id: cloaking-system
name: Cloaking System
order: 2
category: body
# A Factor Trait replaces a Secondary Racial Trait - Secondary, then, unless it names a Primary one to replace.
importance: secondary
description: >
  You have the ability to slip past your enemies’ notice.
text: >
  Cloaking System (Body): You have the ability to slip past your enemies’ notice.
  (1)-[Passive]: Increase the Natural Result of your Stealth Skill Checks by 1.
  (2)-[Passive]: Increase your Wound Rolls by 2(T) against your Oblivious Character(s).
  (3)-[1/Round]: As a Standard Maneuver with an Action Cost of 1 and a Ki Point Cost of 10(bT), enter the Invisible State.
  (4)-[1/Round]: As an Instant Maneuver during your turn, or in response to the end of your turn, leave the Invisible State.
  (5)-[Automatic/Start of Turn]: If you are in the Invisible State due to the 3rd effect of Cloaking System, reduce your Ki Points and Capacity by 8(bT).

---

[passive]
# (1), (2)
skill.stealth.natural += 1;
wound.vsOblivious += 2(T);
# (3), (4) Its own Maneuvers, on the Maneuvers tab (maneuvers/cloaking-system-*.dbu): in, 1 Action and 10(bT) Ki; out, as an Instant,
# once a Round - its mark (Cloaked) saying the Invisible State is Cloaking System's. When in the turn (4) is used, the table's.

# (5) Your turn begins Invisible by Cloaking System: 8(bT) Ki Points and as much Capacity.
[automatic/start-of-turn, effect 5]
requires inState("invisible") && hasCondition("cloaked");
ki.value -= 8(bT);
capacity.spent += 8(bT);

# The Invisible State gone some other way: its mark with it.
[automatic/start-of-turn]
requires hasCondition("cloaked") && !inState("invisible");
remove(cloaked);
